  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al-Atta</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen the resilience of widows, marginalized women, and women with disabilities who are breadwinners in Gaza City and the North. It will support their existing small businesses that were damaged during the recent war or are struggling tocontinue due to lack of capital.
The project will target 15 women from these groups. Each participant will receive cash or in-kind funding ranging between GBP 1,000&#x2013;1,200, depending on the nature and actual needs of her business. The support will cover the purchase of raw materials, operational tools, or working capital to help them restart, expand, and increase their profitability.
This intervention is not only about supporting individual businesses but also about laying the groundwork for a collective development model through production cooperatives. This will contribute to alleviating poverty, promoting economic and social stability, and enhancingwomen&#x2019;s ability to engage confidently and effectively in the local market.
The project will establish small production cooperativesby merging 3&#x2013;4 similar or complementary businesses into shared production or marketing units, managed collaboratively by the participating women. This approach will strengthen their market competitiveness, reduce operational costs, and increase their production and marketing capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">5- AlAtaa Association:

Empowers families and individuals, especially women and youth, to improve their lives and communities. Also, focuses on enhancing education, health, and cultural awareness, providing training and support to help people build skills and confidence. Their goal is to address the challenges faced by marginalized groups, ensuring everyone has the opportunity to participate fully in society and advocate for their rights.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al-Ataa Charitable Society</narrative>
  </participating-org>
